{"parentUuid":"919f2706-720e-4630-b3fd-370c49d5c905","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01CvDLDS4puc5TJikqS9hHux","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"96787e2d-8d10-47ac-bf3f-2a1ca9370303","timestamp":"2026-10-20T21:04:48.215Z","session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"96787e2d-8d10-47ac-bf3f-2a1ca9370303","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgEAfyfRCaeCNqpWGHkLM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W7aaZzHvT7yNGMC8Kvdw2V","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into retrieval-output-correctness\n\n26 hunks across 10 files, all collateral: main has absorbed 20 PRs since this\nbranched, including the removal of semantic retrieval, the hiding of six MCP\naliases, and a rewrite of agent-harness detection. None of the conflicts\ncarried this PR's own feature, so all 26 took main; suppressed_warnings and\nthe retrieval output changes survive untouched in the files that did not\nconflict.\n\nThree test files were left orphaned, each guarding a symbol main deleted.\nRemoved only after confirming the behaviour is still covered:\n\n  partial_clone_index_test.go    stampSemanticHeaderFromLocalGit -> main\n                                 validates instead of stamping; promisor /\n                                 E_NO_GIT_HEAD covered in\n                                 semantic_repokey_consolidated_test.go\n  semantic_partial_clone_test.go annotateSemanticHeaderRefusal, same path\n  refresh_ollama_auto_test.go    ollamaModelMissingWarning -> agent resolution\n                                 rewritten; covered by refresh_test.go,\n                                 install_ux_test.go, agent_policy_test.go\n\nsemantic_stream.go still stamped brain-supplied provenance; main refuses an\nidentity-less snapshot rather than inventing identity for it, so the call and\nits now-dead stampedHeader field are gone.\n\nThen this PR's guards earned their place by finding four real things:\n\n  statusCauseWidth    bundleImportConflictError was 402 characters against a\n                      140 budget, and it is recorded as a freshness axis\n                      detail, so it was clipped mid-sentence everywhere it\n                      appeared. Rewritten to 128, keeping the clause #344's\n                      guard requires -- what --overwrite COSTS. One wording\n                      now satisfies both.\n  MCP cue             main's rewritten brain_query and brain_recall said when\n                      to use them and not when to stop. Both now name a\n                      built-in alternative and carry a \"Not for ...\" clause.\n  stale exemptions    the cue allowlist still exempted brain_index_status and\n                      brain_get_architecture, which #400 removed from the\n                      advertised surface, so those entries exempted nothing.\n  retired field       retired_manifest_field_test.go used \"suppressed_warnings\"\n                      as its RETIRED-field fixture -- the field this PR adds as\n                      real. On main that passes; the moment this lands it would\n                      assert \"retired\" about a live field. Repointed, as\n                      brain_manifest_read_test.go already was.\n\nTwo of this PR's own hook assertions were superseded and are now aligned to\n#402's contract, which is the better one: silence is gated on --claude-hook,\nso the real hook never breaks an agent's edit over an unreadable payload while\na hand-run still says what went wrong.\n\nTestTheHookCallSiteGuardsTheStdinRead grepped hook_cmd.go for\n`hookStdinWouldBlock`. That pinned a NAME: main renamed the predicate to\nstdinIsPipe and inverted it, and the guard went red on correct code. It now\nasserts the behaviour -- a pipe is the harness and must be read, a terminal is\na character device and must not be, and the fast-fail path returns rather than\nreading a stream that never EOFs. My first attempt at that rewrite modelled a\nnever-closing PIPE, which is not what a terminal is; it failed, correctly, and\nis fixed.\n\nMCP golden regenerated and reviewed as a contract change: same 32 tools as\nmain, 20 richer descriptions, nothing added or removed from the surface.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green, every other package green, go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push origin HEAD:fix/retrieval-output-correctness 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]|cannot lock|another git\" | tail -2","description":"Commit and push 329"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":660610,"output_tokens":1451,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1451,"cache_read_input_tokens":660610,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W7aaZzHvT7yNGMC8Kvdw2V":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-v1-retrieval && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge main into retrieval-output-correctness\n\n26 hunks across 10 files, all collateral: main has absorbed 20 PRs since this\nbranched, including the removal of semantic retrieval, the hiding of six MCP\naliases, and a rewrite of agent-harness detection. None of the conflicts\ncarried this PR's own feature, so all 26 took main; suppressed_warnings and\nthe retrieval output changes survive untouched in the files that did not\nconflict.\n\nThree test files were left orphaned, each guarding a symbol main deleted.\nRemoved only after confirming the behaviour is still covered:\n\n  partial_clone_index_test.go    stampSemanticHeaderFromLocalGit -> main\n                                 validates i